Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
include("IncantForms/WorkingOn/parser");
define
    vtFires=0;
    vtSay code={
        v := tell(argument);
        m := *v["matched"]; c := *v["consumed"];
        cerr "   verdict matched= " m " consumed= " c " vetoFires= " vtFires:;
        };
    ;
register(VetoP);
define
    VtOpt isRule vo-="x" code={ vtFires += 1; return null; };
    VcOpt isRule vc-="x";
    ;
define
    VtOUT isRule VtOpt? vr-="x";
    VcOUT isRule VcOpt? vq-="x";
    ;
search GroupFields UnitTests Utilities VetoP list;
cerr "OLD control VcOUT x":;
vtSay("VcOUT x");
cerr "OLD veto    VtOUT x":;
vtSay("VtOUT x");
cerr "OLD control VcOUT xx":;
vtSay("VcOUT xx");
cerr "OLD veto    VtOUT xx":;
vtSay("VtOUT xx");
parser(VtOUT);
parser(VcOUT);
cerr "NEW control VcOUT x":;
vtSay("VcOUT x");
cerr "NEW veto    VtOUT x":;
vtSay("VtOUT x");
cerr "NEW control VcOUT xx":;
vtSay("VcOUT xx");
cerr "NEW veto    VtOUT xx":;
vtSay("VtOUT xx");
cerr "PROBE vetoOptional SENTINEL":;
stop();

vetoOptional -- deepClean D-24 (SEQ 260 R9). sukcess carries both "the action vetoed this match" (fireLabelMethod
sets it false when the action returns null) and "satisfied by min". On the OLD road (parse()) a vetoed iteration
reaches matchFailed, where kount >= min flips it back to true and the rewind inside `if !sukcess` is skipped, so the
vetoed match's input may stay consumed. The NEW road (exitFromParse) rewinds before its min-zero success.
Rows: VcOUT (no action on the optional) is the control and must read the same on both roads. VtOUT's optional
matches "x" and vetoes; if the old road keeps the consumed "x", the literal after it fails there and not on the
new road. The xx rows: the control reads matched 1 consumed 2; a veto that keeps its input consumed reads
consumed 2, one that rewinds reads consumed 1. vetoFires must RISE across a veto row for a veto row to mean anything.
